    "Stages overlap; do not sum. Failed test assumptions and intermediate proof boundaries are retained.",
    "The existing owned ProjectPack catalog remains the default. Registered scope reads only explicitly registered direct dependency Pack manifests; transitive-only registrations do not confer callable selection access.",
    "The dedicated external contract query reads no external implementation/provider body. The ordinary caller graph view still reads its already-owned node sources for preservation and diagnostics. The selected declaration and manifest are read again before owned draft mutation. This is an exact raw receipt fence for that selection, not a filesystem-wide atomic snapshot or final provider selection. Other referenced contracts retain the existing semantic contract-version fence and compiler validation.",
    "The manifest-only catalog is bounded at128 packs,32 rows/page,1MiB/file and2MiB reads. Creation additionally accounts for owned observed source bytes plus selected external manifest/function bytes under the prospective2MiB guard. External declarations never become owned source units.",
    "Pure metadata and private input restoration neither compile nor execute a provider. Explicit graph/import Review and compiler Confirm remain required. All execution uses owned local fixtures.",
    "Same-function object-parent provider reuse is complete and does not require child reimplementation. Existing IMPLEMENTATION_ID refusal for different-function implementation inheritance remains.",
    "No original ZIP, main branch, Android settings, external account, paid model or user PC installation changes. Managed targets only compile; no native/device claim."
